# `fluid::Act`

What an action does to a device.

## Signature

```cpp
fluid::Act
```

## What It Does

The change an `Action` makes. `Close` shuts the link. `Open` reopens it and clears a value that an earlier `Set` had latched, returning the device to its pattern baseline. `Set` opens the device and latches `Action::value`: a relative speed for a pump, the loss coefficient for a throttle valve, the flow for a flow valve, the pressure head for a pressure valve.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `Open` | Reopen the link and release a latched setting. |  |
| `Close` | Shut the link; it carries no flow. |  |
| `Set` | Open the link and latch `value`. |  |

## Returns

An enumeration; `Action::act`.

## Errors

A `Set` value that is invalid for the device is rejected by `run`.

## Interpretation and Use

Actions are persistent: they stay in effect until another action changes the device. Every `Close` needs an `Open` or the device stays closed for the rest of the run.

